From 00e66f418913a07da607328cee1b9982962b8c1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daira-Emma Hopwood <daira@jacaranda.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:29:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] The 147-bit policy and its compression cells

The single policy is the ADPS16 quantum gate at 147 bits, the most that the rank-one compression maps allow at the catalog's geometry: the first map, at ring dimension 16 and width 4,096, certifies at 147.3 bits, where a 150-bit cell allows 3,806. The six compression cells carry the rank-one widths at 147 bits.

The shipped width tables keep their 128-bit widths under the policy's new name, so that the crates build; the estimator's emitters regenerate them at the new floor (euclidean_width_table and infinity_width_table with --format rust-split).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
